{"name":"Stone Ground","hex":"#d39831","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"},{"term":"ground","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The surface of the Earth, as opposed to the sky or water or underground.","Terrain."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To connect (an electrical conductor or device) to a ground.","To electrocute."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ground"}],"entries":[{"title":"Millstone","blocks":[{"text":"Millstones or mill stones are stones used in gristmills, used for triturating, crushing or, more specifically, grinding wheat or other grains. They are sometimes referred to as grindstones or grinding stones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Millstone_Anatomy.jpg/330px-Millstone_Anatomy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millstone","wikidata":"Q670985"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_(geology)","wikidata":"Q8063"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Holgate_Windmill_millstones_-_2011-12-26.jpg/500px-Holgate_Windmill_millstones_-_2011-12-26.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Holgate_Windmill_millstones_-_2011-12-26.jpg/1280px-Holgate_Windmill_millstones_-_2011-12-26.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Holgate_Windmill_millstones_-_2011-12-26.jpg/500px-Holgate_Windmill_millstones_-_2011-12-26.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pair of millstones in Holgate Windmill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHolgate_Windmill_millstones_-_2011-12-26.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/156_Mus%C3%A9e_pr%C3%A9histoire_Penmarc%27h.JPG/500px-156_Mus%C3%A9e_pr%C3%A9histoire_Penmarc%27h.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/156_Mus%C3%A9e_pr%C3%A9histoire_Penmarc%27h.JPG/1280px-156_Mus%C3%A9e_pr%C3%A9histoire_Penmarc%27h.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/156_Mus%C3%A9e_pr%C3%A9histoire_Penmarc%27h.JPG/500px-156_Mus%C3%A9e_pr%C3%A9histoire_Penmarc%27h.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nether millstone and knurling wheel found at the La Torche site (Plomeur)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A156_Mus%C3%A9e_pr%C3%A9histoire_Penmarc'h